## WHAT THE WORK IS
**General property (binding):** *a purchase section gains ONE input member, `PurchaseSection.Sites` (`IReadOnlyList<SiteAllocation>?`, trailing, optional, `[property: JsonIgnore(Condition = JsonIgnoreCondition.WhenWritingNull)]`, default `null`), and the record `SiteAllocation(string Site, int Devices)` is declared in `Input/PurchaseInput.cs`. Nothing else is added to any input or result type. A section that states no sites calculates, hashes and stores byte for byte as at main. A stated allocation changes NO figure, NO line or section status, NO total, NO approval, and no result member: its only effect is (1) the structure check below, which blocks an unusable allocation, and (2) ONE Review issue per group section whose allocated devices do not add up to its fleet quantity N.* Member and code names are English technical; no screen word beyond Q-9's literals.

**The rule table (binding unless Tuesday overrides at the stamp).** Let N = the section's `FleetQuantity`, L = its `Sites`, S = the sum of L's `Devices` as a 64-bit integer (never an unchecked 32-bit sum).
| the section | what happens |
|---|---|
| L is `null` | as main: no check, no issue, same hash, same JSON (Q-4: an empty list `[]` is "no allocation": no check, no issue, but its input hash differs from `null`'s) |
| L stated, section not a group (N `null`) | blocks: code `INVALID SITE ALLOCATION`, target `sections[<id>].sites`, `Priced` false, `Purchase` null (Q-3) |
| L stated, a site name that is null, empty or only white space | blocks: the same code and target (Q-5) |
| L stated, two names equal after trimming, compared ordinal ignoring case | blocks: the same code and target (Q-5) |
| L stated, a site's `Devices` below 0 | blocks: the same code and target (Q-6) |
| L stated and usable, N group, S = N | no issue; every figure and issue as the unset twin |
| L stated and usable, N group, S not equal N (more or fewer) | ONE Review issue: code `SITE ALLOCATION DIFFERS`, target `sections[<id>].sites`, severity Review, the sentence under Q-9 carrying S and N; `Priced` true; every figure as the unset twin (Q-8) |
**Several sections:** one issue per mismatched group section, in section order; a blocked quote carries its Blocking issues and no Review issue of this check. **A site with 0 devices is allowed (Q-6); a group of N 0 with sites summing to 0 raises nothing.** **The comparison is to N, never to a counted device quantity (Q-7):** a group with a `FixedPerGroup` or `Manual` device line (X-41, X-42) has a device quantity that differs from N, and the allocation still adds up to N. **Shape in code (binding):** the structure check goes in the `CheckPurchaseStructure` section loop (:306-336) beside the fleet quantity check, using the existing `Block` local and `t`; the Review check is a new private static method beside `CheckSoftwareTerm`, called after it (:202); the six literals live in `PurchaseRules` (three `public const string`: the two codes and the rule label) or inline as the existing Review issues do; no helper is shared with `Reconciliation`.

- **Edge rows, each a test row in the NEW file, values hand-derived in a comment before the rule exists, SYNTHETIC (`SYN-*` keys, round invented site names such as "Site A"); model the fixture on `DeviceGroupTests.cs` :19-57 and on `ComponentQuantityRuleTests.cs`'s fixtures (read, not edited):**
  **(a) equal:** N 7, sites 3 and 4: no issue with the new code; the whole result equals the unset twin's after removing exactly `calculationId` and `inputHash`; the input hash differs from the twin's. **(b) short:** N 7, sites 3 and 3 (S 6): exactly one issue with the code, severity Review, target `sections[<id>].sites`, `Priced` true, and the sentence once pinned verbatim; every figure equals the twin's. **(c) over:** N 7, sites 3 and 5 (S 8): the same, S 8. **(d) one site, one zero site:** N 5 with one site of 5: nothing; N 5 with sites 5 and 0: nothing; N 5 with one site of 0: one issue (S 0).
  **(e) N 0:** sites 0 and 0: nothing; one site of 1: one issue (S 1, N 0); a section with N 0 and no lines still a group. **(f) the count it compares to (Q-7):** N 4 with a per-device device line q 1 and a `FixedPerGroup` device line q 9 (device quantity 13): sites 1 and 3 (S 4) raise nothing; sites summing to 13 raise one issue; N 4 with a per-device line q 2 (counted 8): sites summing to 4 raise nothing, to 8 raise one issue. These kill a mutant that compares to the section's device quantity or to a line's extended quantity.
  **(g) figures do not move:** over the fixtures of (a) to (f) and a fee fixture (N 4, a stated managed-service fee, sites 1 and 1), the stated-sites result equals the unset twin's in every figure, line, section and quote total, status, usage figure and projection, JSON equal after removing exactly `calculationId`, `inputHash` and the new issue, under InputHash's options and the store's options; the fee stays fee x N (X-38). **(h) the other issues keep their order:** a quote with `OPTION FITS NO DEVICE` and `SOFTWARE TERM MISMATCH` issues plus a mismatched allocation lists the existing issues first, in today's order, and the new one last; the same quote without sites lists exactly the existing issues.
  **(i) not a group:** sites on a section with no fleet quantity: `Priced` false, `Purchase` null, exactly one blocking issue with `INVALID SITE ALLOCATION` at `sections[<id>].sites`; the same section without sites prices. **(j) unusable allocations, each its own row:** a null name, an empty name, a white-space name, two equal names, two names equal ignoring case, two names equal after trimming, a negative device count (-1): each one blocking issue with the code and target, `InputHash.Compute` does not throw on the way. A mismatched allocation and a blocked allocation never appear on one quote: a blocked quote carries no Review issue of this check. Also a negative `FleetQuantity` with sites: the existing `INVALID QUANTITY` at `sections[<id>].fleetQuantity` is present (the new code may or may not appear beside it: STATE which in DESIGN).
  **(k) sum beyond the integer range (B1075-5's shape):** two sites of `int.MaxValue` at N 5: no exception; one Review issue; the sentence carries the true 64-bit sum (4294967294). One site of `int.MaxValue` at N `int.MaxValue`: nothing. These kill a 32-bit or `checked` int sum. **(l) several sections:** three group sections, the first and third mismatched, the second equal: exactly two Review issues, targets the first and third, in section order.
  **(m) the reconciliation is unchanged (B1075-4):** `QuoteReconciler.Reconcile(input, result).Agrees` is true with sites stated, for each of (a), (b), (c), (e), (f), (g), upfront, with a section supplies model, and with deal usage; and `Reconcile(inputWithSites, resultCalculatedWithoutSites).Agrees` is true (a site moves no figure, so either result agrees with either input). **(n) readiness is unchanged:** `ReadinessEvaluator.Evaluate(...)` for the quote with sites equals the evaluator's output for its unset twin, check by check.
  **(o) byte-equal by path:** `sites` absent from every section of an unset quote and of a quote stating `null` under InputHash's options and the store's options; present only at `sections[].sites` on a stated section, under no line, click or usage object; an empty list `[]` is written as `[]` and read back as an empty list (Q-4). **(p) the written shape:** a stated allocation serialises its two members as `site` and `devices` (the camel-cased names the other input members use); round-trip under the store's options: written, read, re-written byte-equal; a head-written record reads at MAIN's binary with no exception and every other member equal (the key is ignored; state what main's binary does with it, measured). **(q) a repeat of the -253 rules beside sites:** a group with each of the three rules on its device lines and sites equal to N: nothing raised, figures equal the unset twin's.
- **Two register rows** (`docs/ENGINE.md`, after X-42, same table form, ASCII, no ticket key; "a group with no allocation is unchanged"; the last cell names the code): **X-43** the member: `PurchaseSection.Sites` and `SiteAllocation(Site, Devices)`; a group's devices may be allocated across named sites; left out of the JSON and the input hash when `null`, so a quote that states no sites calculates, hashes and stores byte for byte as before; an empty list is no allocation and is written as an empty list; a site name is free text, trimmed for the comparison, one name once (ignoring case); a device count is a whole number from 0; a section that is not a group, a blank or repeated name or a negative count is `INVALID SITE ALLOCATION` at `sections[<id>].sites` and prices nothing; **no figure, status or total reads a site**; purchase only (the rental `Site` is a separate free-text label); engine only: the contract and the screens cannot state a site, so every quote made through the Api states none (`PurchaseMapping` builds no sites); `perSite` is still not a quantity rule (X-40). **X-44** the check: on a group whose allocation is usable, the sites' devices are added as 64-bit integers and compared with the group's fleet quantity N (never a line's quantity or the section's device quantity); a different sum raises one Review issue `SITE ALLOCATION DIFFERS` at `sections[<id>].sites` per section, after the quote's other Review issues; a warning only: no price, status, total or approval changes; the independent reconciliation is unchanged and agrees; a quote that is blocked raises none. Say in the row what the result holds (the issue only) and that the calculation id formed from the hash differs from the unset twin's.
- **Sentences this makes false (the only existing doc bytes you may change; each listed before and after in STATUS):** `PurchaseInput.cs` section param comments :49-64: add the `Sites` param comment (an addition, not an edit); any existing comment that says a section has no sites or that a group has only a fleet quantity: measure first with `git grep -n -i -E 'site|fleet quantity|billable device group'` over Yours and say of each hit true / now false (edit) / why. **X-35, X-38, X-40 to X-42 are not edited.** Any other sentence you find false: STOP.
- **Row discipline.** Red-first: add both new types and the member inert (read by nothing, the checks absent), show every behavioural row RED for the right reason at base+inert, then the checks, then green; quote the red per check (structure check, Review check). No `Thread.Sleep`, wall clock, unseeded random, environment read; expected values typed literals hand-derived in a comment; no site name, price, cost, BID, SKU or customer value from any real source. Test names and comments name no ticket, finding, brief, mutant or person; `X43_`, `X44_` prefixes are register ids.
- **BYTE-EQUAL (binding; rebuild it yourself).** A throwaway harness in `.tools/b1080/scratch` (NOT committed) records every result of every caller file at base and at head under THREE serializers (`InputHash`'s private options by reflection, the Api's `ApiJson.Options`, `ReferenceStore.JsonOptions`), nothing stripped; compare per file: whole raw, and whole with only `InputHash`/`CalculationId` masked (mask THEN sort); c0 = base vs base (two builds) shows only the known run-id pair; control: one flipped hex digit fails the compare. **Expected: every shared record equal, because no existing caller states a site; ANY difference is a Blocker-class STOP.** `InputHash.Compute` CALLED on 20 seeded stored-shape purchase and 20 rental inputs, base vs head: 40 of 40 equal; plus 20 purchase inputs stating `Sites = null` explicitly vs unset: 20 of 20 equal; a stated allocation differs on 20 of 20 (the control). **Round trip (`CalculationRecord` under the store's options):** base-era reads at head, re-serialises byte-equal; head-era with `sites` reads at main's binary with no exception and every other member equal.
- **Seeded sweep (binding):** at least 400 quotes (`new Random(seed)`, synthetic). Generator shape stated as a PROPERTY first: group sections N unset and 0..6; `Sites` null, empty, or 1..4 entries from a small name pool (with a share of repeats, blanks, negatives and a non-group section carrying sites); device counts 0..9 and a share of `int.MaxValue`; the -253 line rules {unset, `PerDevice`, `FixedPerGroup`, `Manual`}; q 0..9; optional, credit, included, override; markup and margin; fees; section rates OR deal usage; a share of blocked quotes. Print the census per class. For each: (i) the issue list equals an INDEPENDENT formula read from the INPUT (usable allocation, 64-bit sum, N) and the blocked set equals the independent unusable test; (ii) **metamorphic:** the sites-stripped twin equals the quote in every figure beyond the two hash keys and the new issue; print how many qualified; (iii) a quote with `Sites` null or absent is raw-equal to base; (iv) `sites` present exactly where the table says, by path; (v) `Reconcile` agrees on 100 percent of priced quotes, or the disagreement is a difference base also shows (the X-34 limit of the -253 lane, named by the same shape: any other shape is a finding); (vi) 0 exceptions. Print counts and differences (expected 0). Control: MS1, MS2 and MS15 run through the sweep must report differences, else its zero is NOT EVIDENCE.
- **Red-proof (BINDING, mutants in `wt-b1080-mut` only, run AFTER commit 1 with `wt-b1080-mut` checked out detached at commit 1 (clean tree, so porcelain is 0 before and after each); per mutant: sha256 before, anchor asserted exactly once, edit read back, Release build 0 warnings (a warning is a broken mutant: rewrite it, quarantine the first form), the Engine tests AND your harness sweep run, original bytes written back and sha256 proved equal, `git status --porcelain` 0 lines; predictions with red rows by name written to `.tools/b1080/out/predictions.txt` BEFORE the run). Closed list stated as a PROPERTY: each mutant breaks one clause of the general property, one row of the rule table, or one claim of X-43, X-44 or the commit message; at least these:** **MS1** the Review check removed (no issue ever). **MS2** the comparison against the section's device quantity. **MS3** the comparison against the sum of the lines' extended quantities. **MS4** only "over" raises (S > N). **MS5** only "short" raises (S < N). **MS6** an off-by-one (a sum one above or one below N raises nothing; only a larger difference raises). **MS7** a 32-bit unchecked sum. **MS8** a `checked` 32-bit sum (throws at the int range). **MS9** the check also raises on `null` sites (treats it as S 0). **MS10** the check also raises on an empty list. **MS11** a non-group section with sites is accepted (no block). **MS12** a blank name accepted. **MS13** a duplicate name accepted (exact). **MS14** the duplicate test is case-sensitive only or untrimmed. **MS15** a stated site changes a figure (the fee's devices read S). **MS16** a negative count accepted. **MS17** severity Blocking instead of Review. **MS18** the two codes swapped. **MS19** the target path wrong (`sections[<id>]` without `.sites`). **MS20** one issue per site instead of per section. **MS21** the issue emitted before the existing Review issues (order moves). **MS22** the `JsonIgnore` removed on the input member (an unset quote's hash moves). **MS23** the Review check runs on a blocked quote. **MS24** the sentence's S and N swapped. Any other decision point you find: prove it killed or equivalent or STOP. Controls c0 (no edit) green, c1 (whitespace) same as c0. A mutant nothing kills is reported with the cell that would kill it, and you add that cell in commit 2 (D2) rather than leave it. **A kill by the sweep alone is reported by name and gets a row in commit 2.**

