1. PRIOR-WORK CHECK before you edit (the section above; a READY without a PRIOR WORK section is returned). 2. **Push once** (new branch, under `.tools/.git-lock`, `/bin/bash`, `git -C '<wt-b1080-fix>' push origin HEAD:refs/heads/b1080/mps-257-sites-on-purchase-groups`); never `--force`, a `+refspec`, another ref, or a second push; read back with `ls-remote`. Tuesday opens the PR and lands it after the gate and CodeQL (the Datasec org ruleset is never bypassed, no alert is dismissed). 3. No production, no hosted site, no HTTP to any app host, no `az`, no docker. Nothing deploys. 4. No message to any human, no Jira write, no PR comment. No person's name, decision-card id, finding id, mutant id, brief number or Jira key in code, commit messages or test names (STATUS may). Pricebook data is confidential: SYNTHETIC values only. Never open `2_Project_Files/.local/`, `1_Project_Definition/Source_Documents/**`, `inbound/`, customer price files, `.tools/backup-*`, `.tools/qa-*` or another seat's `.tools/*` tree. 5. **Never delete** (`rm`, `rm -rf` even of your own scratch, `git branch -d`, `--prune`, `update-ref -d`, `worktree prune`, `gc`, `reset`, `clean`, `stash`); quarantine by MOVE to `.tools/_quarantine/2026-11-02_B1080_<what>/` (the one exception: `rmdir` of your own EMPTY lock directory). Existing assertions, rows and files are never deleted or loosened. **Git writes in the code repo are exactly:** the one fetch, two `worktree add --detach`, `checkout --detach <commit 1 or 2>` inside `wt-b1080-mut` only, `git add` of Yours paths and commits in `wt-b1080-fix`, the one push. Any other (including `add -N`): STOP. 6. **Shell:** never type `cd` (not in scripts either); absolute single-quoted paths (they hold a space and `!`); every scratch and tmp file under `.tools/b1080/` or `TMPDIR=/private/tmp/b1080-seat-tmp`, never elsewhere under `/private/tmp`; `git -C` with `--no-optional-locks` for reads; `/usr/bin/grep -i` with a positive control for every count; `python3 -I -B`